{"id":85675636143125,"type":"album","name":"Lost in the Dream","artist":"The War on Drugs","year":2014,"weight":12,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/11625-lost-in-the-dream_004631.jpg","aoty":85,"aoty_user":82,"yt":"Lq_vlKanDKY","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-war-on-drugs/lost-in-the-dream","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/11625-the-war-on-drugs-lost-in-the-dream.php"},"desc":"Lost In The Dream is the third album by Philadelphia band The War on Drugs, but in many ways, it feels like the first. Around the release of the 2011 breakthrough Slave Ambient, Adam Granduciel spent the bulk of two years on the road, touring through progressively larger rock clubs, festival stages and late-night television slots. As these dozen songs shifted and grew beyond what they'd been in the studio, The War on Drugs became a bona fide rock 'n' roll band. That essence drives Lost In The Dream, a 10-song set produced by Granduciel and longtime engineer Jeff Zeigler. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":36400319496976,"name":"The War on Drugs","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":106381401668595,"type":"genre","name":"Heartland Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":254,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"}],"lists":[{"id":115932688871073,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Heartland Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":11,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":23977543053176,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 2014","src":"musthear","grp":"sputnikmusic","list_year":null,"rank":43,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":50254398381317,"name":"Pitchfork: The 200 Best Albums of the 2010s","src":"musthear","grp":"musicbrainz","list_year":null,"rank":97,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":84472050122582,"name":"AOTY Must He